🌐 HTTP and WWW Simulation: Web Server Interaction
🎯 Objective
To implement and simulate the Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) within a Cisco Packet Tracer environment, demonstrating how web servers and clients interact to transfer content over the World Wide Web (WWW) .

📘 Theory
📨 HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol)
An application-layer protocol that follows a Request-Response model. It typically runs over TCP on Port 80.

🖥️ Web Client
A browser that initiates an HTTP GET request to a specific IP address or domain name.

🗄️ Web Server
A host that listens for requests and responds with resources such as HTML files, images, stylesheets, and scripts.

🖧 Topology Setup
Device	IP Address	Role
Web Server	192.168.1.1	Configured with custom index.html
Client PC0	192.168.1.2	Web browser client
Client PC1	192.168.1.3	Web browser client
Switch	—	Cisco 2960 Switch (Star Topology)
Connecting Device: Cisco 2960 Switch connecting all devices in a Star Topology.

🔍 Simulation Steps
1. ✅ Connectivity Test
Ensure all devices can ping the web server successfully.

2. 🌍 Web Access
Use the PC's Web Browser tool to request:
➡️ http://192.168.1.1

3. 📦 Packet Analysis
Use Simulation Mode to capture and inspect:

Direction	Message
Client → Server	HTTP GET request
Server → Client	HTTP 200 OK response
